// A constant may not hold a value that owns a resource: it can neither
// freeze one (a half-usable File) nor copy one (two owners of one
// descriptor). The compiler refuses every binding whose STATIC type can hold
// one -- and a lambda's never can, because a lambda's static type is always
// an interface, which the walk stops at. So this is the case the runtime
// backstop exists for, and the captured `Res` is found by the walk over the
// unfrozen graph before anything is frozen.
interface Get { int of(); }
type Res { int id; }
void Res.drop() { print("closed"); }
int Res.id_of() { return id; }

void go() {
  Res r = Res(7);
  const Get g = () => r.id_of();
  print(g.of());
}
go();
